 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Homogeneous Regions:** The gradient vector, often used as the surface normal in volume rendering, is not well-defined in homogeneous regions where the gradient magnitude is near zero. This can lead to undefined normals and incorrect shading. A common modification is to shade only regions with high gradient magnitudes [S1, book][S8].
