 *   **Local Illumination Limitations:** The model ignores indirect light, shadows, and global effects, which can result in unrealistic lighting in complex scenes [S1, book][S8].
-*   **Numerical Precision:** In homogeneous regions, floating-point cancellation can occur when computing the gradient. Using a threshold to ignore low-magnitude gradients is recommended [S1, book][S8].
-*   **Half-Vector Calculation:** If $\mathbf{l}$ and $\mathbf{v}$ are nearly opposite, $\mathbf{h}$ may become unstable. Normalization handles this, but care should be taken with very small angles [S3, unofficial].
