 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per surface point/sample. The computation involves a few vector operations (dot products, normalization, power function) and is independent of the number of lights or scene complexity, assuming a fixed number of lights.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per sample, storing only temporary vectors and scalars.
-*   **Measured Performance:** Very fast, suitable for real-time rendering. The simplicity of the calculation allows it to be executed efficiently in fragment shaders [S1, book][S7, unofficial].
-*   **Scaling:** Performance does not degrade with scene complexity, but adding more lights increases the number of Blinn-Phong evaluations linearly.
